#[summary("한 갈래에서만 옮긴 값은 다른 갈래 끝에서 해제된다(ADR-0081, 백로그 2O-07)")]
mod bd {
    struct Pt { x: i64, y: i64 }

    struct Pair { a: Box<Pt>, b: Box<Pt> }

    enum Pick { First, Second, Neither }

    #[effects(pure)]
    fn mk(x: i64) -> Box<Pt> {
        Box::new(Pt { x: x, y: x.wrapping_mul(10) })
    }

    #[effects(pure)]
    fn take(p: Box<Pt>) -> i64 {
        p.x.wrapping_add(p.y)
    }

    // `p` moves on the then path only: the else path drops it.
    #[effects(pure)]
    fn one_branch(c: bool, x: i64) -> i64 {
        let p: Box<Pt> = mk(x);
        if c { take(p) } else { 0 }
    }

    // Moved on two arms of three: the third drops it.
    #[effects(pure)]
    fn arms(k: Pick, x: i64) -> i64 {
        let p: Box<Pt> = mk(x);
        let q: Box<Pt> = mk(x.wrapping_add(1));
        match k {
            Pick::First => take(p),
            Pick::Second => take(q),
            Pick::Neither => -1,
        }
    }

    // One field moves on one path; the other path drops that field, and the
    // rest of the struct is dropped at the end of the block either way.
    #[effects(pure)]
    fn field(c: bool, x: i64) -> i64 {
        let s: Pair = Pair { a: mk(x), b: mk(x.wrapping_add(2)) };
        let r: i64 = if c { take(s.a) } else { s.b.x };
        r
    }

    #[effects(io)]
    fn main() -> () {
        print_i64(one_branch(true, 1));
        print_i64(one_branch(false, 2));
        print_i64(arms(Pick::First, 3));
        print_i64(arms(Pick::Second, 4));
        print_i64(arms(Pick::Neither, 5));
        print_i64(field(true, 6));
        print_i64(field(false, 7));
    }
}
